(D2 — Discrepancy 2 repro (wrong-value half): on 0.4.9 and earlier, a
 `map` parameter's `'s size` and `'s length` both returned -1, while the
 same map read at top level returned 2. Element access through the
 parameter (`lookup's "ann"`) was already correct, so it was the
 size/length property specifically that was wrong.
 LANGUAGE.md:782 says a typed parameter "supports the same properties
 and operations as a top-level variable of that type".
 The `a float called pad` line is load-bearing on 0.4.9: without a float
 somewhere in the program the same code did not assemble at all — see
 D2b.vox.
 RESOLVED, 2026-08-22 — vox #76 ("the declared-type to codegen-type
 table had been copied out four times and `map` had reached only the
 declaration's copy... The four copies are now one
 `vartype_of_declared_type`"). Re-run verbatim against 0.4.10: the
 through-the-parameter block now matches the top-level block exactly.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D2.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   2
   2
   30
   --- through the parameter ---
   2
   2
   30
